WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.493 --> 00:00:01.464
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

2
00:00:02.188 --> 00:00:05.576
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> An adjective you can use to describe food.

3
00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:08.027
It means that it’s good for you.

4
00:00:10.906 --> 00:00:11.728
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

5
00:00:12.403 --> 00:00:17.338
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> For example, sun, rain, wind, and fog.

6
00:00:17.732 --> 00:00:21.368
This is very important for farmers when they are growing food.

7
00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:25.760
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

8
00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:30.415
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> For example, breakfast, lunch, or dinner.

9
00:00:33.129 --> 00:00:34.182
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

10
00:00:34.856 --> 00:00:38.837
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Some fish live in rivers, but most fish live here.

11
00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:42.686
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

12
00:00:43.426 --> 00:00:45.845
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The opposite of difficult.

13
00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:49.842
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

14
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.819
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The opposite of expensive.

15
00:00:55.615 --> 00:00:56.685
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

16
00:00:57.293 --> 00:01:00.419
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> A short pause when you stop and rest,

17
00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:03.610
and maybe have a coffee or something to eat.

18
00:01:06.489 --> 00:01:07.591
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8

19
00:01:08.265 --> 00:01:10.469
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Another word for <i>very good</i>.